Modifications for Kilim, September and October 2026 (src/auction/EnglishAuction.sol):
- Extract the ascending-bid predicate and adapt the bid state-transition flow.
- Replace marketplace storage and roles with one immutable auction.
- Take bids in native ETH only, with msg.value equal to the bid and no currency wrapper.
- Open bidding only after 100 wallets register, directly or by an EIP-712 / ERC-1271 signature.
- Refund the outbid bidder inside the new bid through a gas-capped call, with a withdrawable
  refund when that call fails.
- Use OpenZeppelin ReentrancyGuard, EIP712, SignatureChecker and Math.
- Add whole-unit bids and uint128 bounds; start the clock at the first bid and extend it on
  late bids with no absolute deadline.
- Separate settlement, prize delivery, rewards and proceeds withdrawal.
- Omit buyouts, wrappers, fees, royalties, forwarding and upgrades.

Only the _isNewWinningBid function is unchanged except whitespace. The surrounding
implementation is extensively modified. Neither the upstream audit nor this
attribution certifies the Kilim adaptation or its reward/composition extensions.

